comments.body:
`lem:miraPiSmall` (§3) invokes, for generic irreducible $\pi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_n$: injectivity of $V\mapsto V|_{P_n}$ and surjectivity of its image onto $\mathcal C_c^\infty(N_n\backslash P_n,\psi)$. The proof merely says "the same Bernstein–Zelevinsky/Kirillov statement as Lemma 1 ... References as in Lemma 1."

This deferral is not acceptable under Grounding. The $\mathrm{GL}_n$ statement must be given explicitly:
- genericity of $\pi$ $\Rightarrow$ highest derivative $\pi^{(n)}\neq0$;
- hence the bottom BZ submodule of $\pi|_{P_n}$ is $\operatorname{ind}_{N_n}^{P_n}\psi=\mathcal C_c^\infty(N_n\backslash P_n,\psi)$, realized inside $\mathcal W(\pi,\psi)|_{P_n}$;
- restriction to $P_n$ is injective.

The genericity hypothesis on $\pi$ (given in the problem) must be **explicitly used** — for non-generic $\pi$ the highest derivative may vanish and surjectivity onto $\mathcal C_c^\infty(N_n\backslash P_n,\psi)$ can fail. State this dependence rather than inheriting it implicitly from Lemma 1.
